---
name: data-driven
description: Data-driven testing with Scenario Outlines and Examples tables
keywords: [data-driven, outline, examples, parameterized, table-driven, 数据驱动]
---

## Applicable Scenarios
- Testing the same flow with multiple input combinations
- Role-based permission matrices
- Multi-language/locale testing
- Pricing/tier-based behavior variations

## Recommended Structure
Use Scenario Outline with Examples tables to cover multiple combinations without repeating steps.

## Example Pattern
```gherkin
Scenario Outline: <role> can access <page>
    Given I am logged in as <role>
    When I navigate to <page>
    Then I should see the page title "<title>"

    Examples:
        | role     | page        | title          |
        | admin    | /admin      | Admin Panel    |
        | user     | /dashboard  | My Dashboard   |
        | guest    | /login      | Sign In        |
```

## Best Practices
1. Use descriptive column names in Examples headers
2. Keep placeholder names short and clear: `<email>` not `<email_address_for_user>`
3. Use Scenario Outline when the same steps apply to 3+ data variations
4. Add edge case rows (null, empty, boundary) to Examples tables
5. Tag each Scenario Outline with the variant dimensions being tested

## Suggested Tags
